# Your own data — never commit this.
#
# artifacts/ holds what the system has learned from YOUR sessions:
#   hint-log.jsonl   every hint shown, with the prior session it pointed at
#   injections/      the full text delivered to the agent, including real
#                    repository names and absolute file paths
#   proposals/       the hint currently displayed in each chat
#   settings.json    your local configuration
#
# Verified to contain real repository names and real file paths.
artifacts/

# Generated test databases — about 23 MB, rebuilt with `node local/build.mjs`.
# Committing them would mean large binary diffs on every regeneration, for data
# that is reproducible byte for byte from the source files.
#
# Two rules on purpose. The folder rule is the clear one; the *.db rule is a
# safety net, because renaming this folder once already silently un-ignored
# 23 MB of databases.
test/db/
local/db/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Retrieval experiments and their fixtures — kept on this machine, not shipped.
#
# These measure the keyword-retrieval system that preference learning replaces:
# the Group A suite, the fixture generators, and the read-only probes that were
# run against the real session store. They stay because the measurements are
# the reasoning behind decisions recorded elsewhere, and because some of them
# read personal session data.
local/

# Planning and evaluation notes — kept local.
#
# These are working documents rather than project documentation. They stay on
# your machine; nothing else depends on them.
#
# Note: adding a path here does NOT untrack files already committed. These were
# committed once, so they also had to be removed with:
#   git rm -r --cached docs
docs/

node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
